    {
      "id": "38137402",
      "title": "About the \"App Router\"",
      "lectureOrder": 421,
      "videoOrder": 388,
      "sourceHash": "7d10bcb76fd97e1dd6972550b0137f343854d093c823ca58f66f38e19179ace5",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 3.48,
          "en": "Now before we start digging",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.48,
          "end": 6.42,
          "en": "into the created project and before we start diving",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.42,
          "end": 9.9,
          "en": "into all these core NextJS features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.9,
          "end": 13.56,
          "en": "I want to come back to this project creation process,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.56,
          "end": 16.29,
          "en": "and there to this question here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.29,
          "end": 19.83,
          "en": "whether we want to use the App Router or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.83,
          "end": 23.73,
          "en": "And here it of course said that it's recommended to use it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.73,
          "end": 26.82,
          "en": "but nonetheless, I told you to choose no.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.82,
          "end": 30.3,
          "en": "Now this approach where you use the App Router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.3,
          "end": 34.35,
          "en": "is an alternative way of building NextJS apps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.35,
          "end": 37.08,
          "en": "An alternative to using the Pages Router,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.08,
          "end": 39.43,
          "en": "which is the approach we'll use in this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.41,
          "end": 43.86,
          "en": "The App Router uses a different project structure,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.86,
          "end": 47.25,
          "en": "a different folder structure, and different features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.25,
          "end": 48.45,
          "en": "The problem with it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.45,
          "end": 52.53,
          "en": "just is that despite the NextJS page telling you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.53,
          "end": 55.05,
          "en": "that it's stable to use now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.05,
          "end": 57.12,
          "en": "crucial features are missing there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.12,
          "end": 60.96,
          "en": "To be precise, this Server Actions feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.96,
          "end": 64.77,
          "en": "is still in Alpha at this point of time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.77,
          "end": 68.88,
          "en": "Now, Server Actions is a part of this App Router feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.88,
          "end": 71.34,
          "en": "even though it's not clearly stated here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.34,
          "end": 73.89,
          "en": "but it is crucial for using the App Router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.89,
          "end": 76.17,
          "en": "because this Server Actions feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.17,
          "end": 78.53999999999999,
          "en": "is a feature that will allow you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.53999999999999,
          "end": 82.14,
          "en": "to basically handle POST, PUT, PATCH,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.14,
          "end": 86.91,
          "en": "basically all non-GET requests in your NextJS app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.91,
          "end": 91.26,
          "en": "So if you wanna build a NextJS app where data can change,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.26,
          "end": 94.92,
          "en": "where users can submit forms, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.92,
          "end": 97.25999999999999,
          "en": "you will need these Server Actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.25999999999999,
          "end": 100.05,
          "en": "to handle these changes on the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.05,
          "end": 103.08,
          "en": "Right now, this feature is not final yet though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.08,
          "end": 105.03,
          "en": "and therefore likely to change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.03,
          "end": 107.67,
          "en": "and likely to contain bugs and errors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107.67,
          "end": 110.88,
          "en": "and it's definitely not recommended for production yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.88,
          "end": 114.12,
          "en": "Therefore, at the moment, with this App Router,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 114.12,
          "end": 116.75999999999999,
          "en": "you can only build basic websites",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 116.75999999999999,
          "end": 119.82,
          "en": "that don't need to handle form submissions and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 119.82,
          "end": 122.43,
          "en": "That's why in the official docs for the App Router,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.43,
          "end": 125.55,
          "en": "you also find no entry for manipulating data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 125.55,
          "end": 127.263,
          "en": "just for data fetching.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.172,
          "end": 129.33,
          "en": "And because of that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 129.33,
          "end": 133.26,
          "en": "this course currently does not cover the App Router yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 133.26,
          "end": 136.8,
          "en": "This, of course, very likely will change in the future.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 136.8,
          "end": 139.47,
          "en": "I do plan to update this course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 139.47,
          "end": 141.9,
          "en": "and give you this update for free",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 141.9,
          "end": 144.75,
          "en": "once this App Router is fully usable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 144.75,
          "end": 146.88,
          "en": "So once all features you need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 146.88,
          "end": 150.27,
          "en": "to build production-ready apps with the App Router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 150.27,
          "end": 151.56,
          "en": "are available.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 151.56,
          "end": 155.43,
          "en": "But until then, this course will use the Pages Router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 155.43,
          "end": 157.17000000000002,
          "en": "And that's why I recommended",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 157.17000000000002,
          "end": 160.82999999999998,
          "en": "that you should not use Yes here when creating the project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 160.82999999999998,
          "end": 165.123,
          "en": "and you were asked to use the App Router, but No instead.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
